---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
const title = "What Is Simple Text Formatting (Markdown)? A Plain Guide - Toolkit Lab";
const description = "What Markdown is, the basic syntax for headings, bold text, links and lists, and where it is used for notes, documentation and websites.";
---
<Base title={title} description={description} path="/guides/what-is-markdown.html">
  <aside class="ad-rail" aria-label="Advertisement"><div class="ad-slot ad-slot-rail"></div></aside>
  <div class="wrap article">
    <p class="note"><a href="/guides.html">Guides</a> / Writing tools</p>
    <h1>What Is Simple Text Formatting (Markdown)? A Plain Guide</h1>
    <p class="lead">Markdown is a simple way to add headings, bold text and links while you type plain text. It is used in notes, documents and websites. This guide explains it in plain terms.</p>
    <div class="ad-slot" aria-label="Advertisement"></div>
<h2>Writing with simple symbols</h2>
<p>Markdown lets you add formatting by typing a few easy symbols. A hash sign at the start of a line makes a heading. Two stars around a word make it bold. Square brackets with a web address make a link.</p>
<h2>Why people use it</h2>
<p>It is quick to type, works on any device, and can be turned into a web page or a document easily. Many note apps and websites accept it.</p>
<h2>Try it yourself</h2>
<p>Type a few lines with a heading and a bold word into the preview. The formatted version shows on the right as you type.</p>
      <section class="worked">
        <h2>Worked example</h2>
        <p>Typing '# My Holiday' makes a large heading. Typing '**Packing list**' makes bold words. Typing '[our site](https://www.toolkitlab.xyz)' makes a link you can click.</p>
      </section>
      <section class="faq-list">
        <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
        <details><summary>How do I type a real asterisk?</summary><p>Put a backslash in front of it, so it shows as a symbol rather than making text bold.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Why did my line breaks disappear?</summary><p>A single line break is often joined to the line above. Leave an empty line to start a new paragraph.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Will every program show these symbols the same way?</summary><p>Most do, but some show less. Check the result in the program you will use.</p></details>
      </section>
      <script is:inline type="application/ld+json">{"@context": "https://schema.org", "@type": "FAQPage", "mainEntity": [{"@type": "Question", "name": "How do I type a real asterisk?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Put a backslash in front of it, so it shows as a symbol rather than making text bold."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Why did my line breaks disappear?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "A single line break is often joined to the line above. Leave an empty line to start a new paragraph."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Will every program show these symbols the same way?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Most do, but some show less. Check the result in the program you will use."}}]}</script>
